    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0704" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756.5–MAP/7–951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Indonesia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-07-13T18:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1951—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Urtel 29 July 9.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d401-f1"/>
                    Indo Amb has not requested reimbursable mil aid
                    for Indo under Sec 408 E MDAP.</p>
                <p>
                    Indo Emb has requested priority assistance (DO
                    rating) on nr contracts for mil forces. However, pending inclusion rubber by
                        Indo in list goods considered covered by
                        UN res Dept has neither taken extraordinary
                    efforts to prevent nor extraordinary efforts to assist in procurement goods in
                    US. Under this policy Dept has for some time withheld approval priority
                    assistance for number Indo contracts with US
                    firms. When satis response assured Dept notified Munitions Board its <pb
                        facs="0705" n="687" xml:id="pg687"/> approval issuance necessary DO’s 825
                    radio sets (SCR–694) for Indo Army. These
                    orders in process issuance. Dept also urging favorable consideration DO covering
                    industrial hand tools, 35 battery chargers, 20 water clarators (purifiers), 150
                    motorcycles and 75 sets motorcycle spare parts. Two orders tires and tubes and
                    126,000 feet subterranean telephone cable being actively studied. Separate tel
                    fol on subject tires.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d401-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d401-f1" n="1" xml:id="d401-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 29 from Djakarta, July 9, Ambassador Cochran reported that he had
                    been informed that Ambassador Sastroamidjojo had been instructed to ask for
                    reimbursable military aid for the Indonesian National Police
                    (756D.5–MAP/7–951).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d401-f2" n="2" xml:id="d401-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
